<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamsui</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Danshui</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamsui is a coastal district of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taipei">Taipei</a> at the mouth of the Tamsui River in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>. The Spanish built Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> there in 1628, later rebuilt by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, whose Fort Antonio still stands. In the 1860s Tamsui became a treaty port with a British consulate, and the Canadian missionary George Leslie Mackay founded schools and a hospital there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamsui.jpg" alt="Tamsui" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sdfery · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%B4%85%E6%AF%9B%E5%9F%8E%E4%B9%8B%E7%BE%8E.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
